.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH dotman-diff 1  "diff "
.SH NAME
dotman\-diff \- Show how $HOME differs from the repo, as a diff from repo/ to home/
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBdotman diff\fR [\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-\-verbose\fR] [\fB\-q\fR|\fB\-\-quiet\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-pager\fR] [\fB\-\-allow\-root\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fIPATHS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Show how $HOME differs from the repo, as a diff from repo/ to home/
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
[\fIPATHS\fR]
Compare only these files or directories; every managed path when none are given
.SH "GLOBAL OPTIONS"
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
Show verbose output
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-quiet\fR
Suppress informational messages
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-pager\fR
Disable pager output
.TP
\fB\-\-allow\-root\fR
Allow running as root
.SH EXTRA
The diff runs from repo/<key> to home/<key>, so an edit made in $HOME shows
as added lines. It goes through git\*(Aqs pager unless \-\-no\-pager or NO_PAGER
is set, or the pager cannot be found. NO_COLOR turns colour off.
